# End-to-end bug fixes

When fixing a reported bug, treat the ticket as a full user flow, not a one-line patch.

- Fix **every action on that screen** that shares the same root cause (e.g. Verify **and** Return to employee **and** Send back to Finance if they share one POST).
- Trace **UI click → fetch headers/body → Flask parse → permission/status → DB write → success toast → timeline/status on reload**.
- JSON POSTs must send `Content-Type: application/json`. FormData uploads must not. Server review endpoints must parse JSON even if the header is missing (`force=True` / raw body).
- Do not leave sibling buttons, routes (`/api/accounts` vs `/api/finance`), or empty/error states unfixed.
- Prefer a success path the tester can complete: enabled controls, real data, user-facing success copy, status/history updated.
- After a fix, mentally re-run the ticket steps and the inverse (logout, refresh, other role, no file, missing remark).
- Do not stop at a generic 400. If testers see a warning toast, match that exact message in code before changing it.
